{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a copy of the attributed string whose image attachments the RTFD format represents","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"faithfully. Use it before you export an attributed string with images, such as the diagrams","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and formulas of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathAttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", as an RTFD document","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"fileWrapper(from:documentAttributes:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the document type ","type":"text"},{"code":"rtfd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). This is what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownUtil/rtfd(_:title:author:maxImageWidth:mermaid:math:imageBaseUrl:renderingOptions:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Foundation","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Foundation/NSAttributedString"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Foundation/NSAttributedString/preparedForRTFD()"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"extendedModule":"Foundation","externalID":"s:So18NSAttributedStringC11MarkdownKitE15preparedForRTFDAByF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"preparedForRTFD"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSAttributedString","text":"NSAttributedString"}],"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit","relatedModules":["Foundation"]}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","title":"preparedForRTFD()"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"preparedForRTFD"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSAttributedString","text":"NSAttributedString"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConvertingMarkdownIntoDocuments","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathematicalFormulas"]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The RTFD format has no room for some of what an attachment says, and a viewer shows an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"image in a different way than a text view does. For every attachment that has PNG data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or any other image data that the system can read) and a size, the copy makes up for this:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The size of an image in an RTFD document results from the resolution of its file, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the ","type":"text"},{"code":"bounds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of its attachment. The image of the copy has a resolution which makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it as large in points as the bounds say.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A viewer places an image on the baseline of the text, since the format does not keep the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertical position of the bounds of an attachment (","type":"text"},{"code":"bounds.origin.y","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). The copy has the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position in the attribute ","type":"text"},{"code":"baselineOffset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the format keeps, so that a formula","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within a line stays aligned with the text.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The files of the images have names that say what they are: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Formula 1.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a formula","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MathAttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Foundation/NSAttributedString/Key/mathSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image 1.png","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for any other image.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The numbers and bullets of list items sit on the baseline of the first line of their items,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also if a formula or another image makes that line taller than the text: a viewer lays out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an image that is lowered by ","type":"text"},{"code":"baselineOffset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" differently than a text view, so the copy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lowers the markers again, for a text of 30 times the font size (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/alignListMarkers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The attachments of the copy are new objects: neither the attributed string nor its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attachments are changed. Attachments without data or without a size are left as they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are, and so is the rest of the string, except for the markers of lists.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let document = try string.preparedForRTFD()","      .fileWrapper(from: NSRange(location: 0, length: string.length),","                   documentAttributes: [.documentType: NSAttributedString.DocumentType.rtfd])"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects that are used in macOS and iOS for displaying rich text.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override how individual Markdown structures are converted into attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/alignListMarkers":{"abstract":[{"text":"If true, the numbers and bullets of list items sit on the baseline of the first line of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their items, also if an image (such as a formula) makes that line taller than the text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(macOS and iOS; the default is ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"alignListMarkers"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/alignListMarkers","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"alignListMarkers","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/alignlistmarkers"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConvertingMarkdownIntoDocuments":{"abstract":[{"text":"Turn a Markdown document into text, HTML, RTF, RTFD or PDF with one call.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ConvertingMarkdownIntoDocuments","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Converting Markdown into Documents","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/convertingmarkdownintodocuments"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show a Markdown document in a SwiftUI view, and adapt it to light and dark mode.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Displaying Markdown with SwiftUI","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/displayingmarkdownwithswiftui"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show fenced code blocks with the language ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"code